    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • This Batmobile-Looking Lamborghini Temerario Is on Display at SEMA\nCheapest CGI Audi Q9 Has Plastic Bumpers, Black Steelies, Manual Tranny, Cloth Seats, Analog Dials\n7 photos\nPhoto: kelsonik / Instagram\nAudi has gone down in preferences for the American customers over the past few months – the sales are showing a 15% drop during the third quarter of the year and an even higher 16% slide year-to-date, after nine months.\nThe problem is that Audi didn’t sign off on 2025 as a record year and didn’t even have a positive outlook. But no worries, as the company has faith in its North American operations thanks to the introduction of brand-new models like the A5 and A6 series, which surged 21% and 24% during the nine months, and also just started selling the all-new Q7 along with the first-ever Q9 full-size three-row crossover SUV.\nThe latter two will probably impact the charts beginning with next year after they ramp up across dealerships, but Audi wants even more – they announced at the end of October 2026 a long-term commitment with a massive US production site in Georgia worth about $4 billion and some 4,500 new jobs. It will focus, beginning in 2030, on its premium “SUVs tailored to North American customers,” which most likely means the likes of Audi’s Q7 and Q9 will have a second home alongside the Volkswagen Bratislava Plant in Slovakia.\nCurrently, the all-new 2027 Audi Q7 and the larger Q9 are starting at $70,900 for the Q7, $98,700 for the SQ7, and $87,700 or $118k for the Q9 and SQ9, respectively. That’s a lot of cash and nobody can promise that once they are getting made locally the prices will go down – inflation tends to erode these expectations. So, what’s the solution for a more accessible Audi Q9, for example?\nWell, a member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators dwelling across the parallel universes of vehicular has a proposition in his latest unofficial, hypothetical design project. More precisely, Nikita Chuicko, the virtual artist better known as \" kelsonik \" on social media, thinks that now is the right CGI time to work on the new 2027 Audi Q9 SUV and make it part of his new CGI Pure Stock series.\nHe previously worked on models like the Mercedes- AMG GT SUV , Jaguar Type 01, G50 BMW 3 Series, Bentley Torcal, or the G65 BMW X5, among others. There was also a CGI Pure Stock 2027 Audi Q7, so, of course, now it’s also the ripe time for the same CGI treatment to be applied to the larger 2027 Audi Q9.\nThe base 2027 Audi Q9, in his vision, comes dressed in non-metallic white, which is now the default free color for many brands, and also has a black plastic grille, black roof rails, black window surrounds, black mirror caps, black door handles, along with black bumpers, side sills, and fender surrounds. At least we’re left with the front and rear LED lights and the color-matching roof spoiler.\nInside, the stock Q9 would make any classic SUV enthusiast blush with excitement: gone is the triple-screen setup and the fancy leather upholstery. In their place now resides a completely different cockpit experience. More precisely, the pixel master has opted for classic round-dial Audi analog instruments for the driver’s cluster, a bezel-heavy and small central screen, separate manual climate controls, and a six-speed manual transmission plus cloth upholstery.\nThere’s even a manual handbrake lever, as well as what looks like recycled materials on the door cards. What do you think – yay or nay? Would you buy something like this? View this post on Instagram A post shared by CAR DESIGN | RENDERINGS (@kelsonik)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\naudi q9 Audi q9 full-size SUV pure stock CGI base specification rendering kelsonik\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1963 Chevrolet Sitting on a Trailer Beg for Restoration if You Don't Get Scared Easily",
